Kind: ablation
Issue: #912
Takes out: the set-associative inode cache -- one way a set, and the 16 slots of ino & 15 it had, whatever table the mount was given: / (inode 2) and /mach_servers (18) evict each other in every walk.  ext_server's check finds /mach_servers/cow_test walked 2000 times reading the inode table after the first walk, and inodes 2, 18, 34, 50, 66 and 82 reading it after the first round.
Run: --entry 14 600 -smp 4
Expect: ext2: inode cache: WRONG -- (/mach_servers/cow_test walked 2000 times read the inode table|inodes 2, 18, 34, 50, 66 and 82 read in turn 50 times read the inode table)

diff --git a/uros/src/file_systems/ext2fs/ext2fs.c b/uros/src/file_systems/ext2fs/ext2fs.c
index 07782631..c266a5d0 100644
--- a/uros/src/file_systems/ext2fs/ext2fs.c
+++ b/uros/src/file_systems/ext2fs/ext2fs.c
@@ -557,7 +557,7 @@ static int write_super(
